{"id": "port-pier-23-rent-and-rebid", "title": "Pier 23’s rent deal reverses the order of two options between official documents", "seconds": 76.8, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.066, "made": "2026-11-27", "key": "19e7a7f3d501a495", "words": 241, "beats": [{"scene": "lease", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "San Francisco’s Port proposed a new Pier 23 lease without a rebid.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.96, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["What", "would", "the", "Port", "collect?"], "sub": "Pier 23 lease"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.87, 1.14, 1.52, 1.6, 1.8, 2.06, 2.68, 2.92, 3.23, 3.31]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 4.08, "t1": 5.73, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A lead, not a finding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.3, 0.4, 0.97, 1.16, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The analyst counted 728,614 dollars in unpaid rent, interest and fees by September 2026.", "t0": 5.85, "t1": 12.7, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$728,614", "label": "Unpaid rent as of September 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.53, 0.87, 1.16, 1.4, 1.85, 2.25, 2.48, 2.72, 3.15, 3.5, 3.62, 4.03, 4.41, 4.79, 4.92, 5.29, 5.46, 5.96, 6.23]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The draft makes forgiveness of those arrears conditional on the first lease extension.", "t0": 12.82, "t1": 16.59, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "lease", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors, file 260948", "text": "Lease extension terms", "mark": "Lease extension terms"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 0.63, 1.21, 1.31, 1.54, 1.93, 2.48, 2.58, 2.69, 2.97, 3.21]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The first extension required $150,000 in qualifying improvements.", "t0": 16.71, "t1": 20.85, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "Tenant improvements", "heading": "Improvements tied to extensions", "source": "lease", "rows": [{"icon": "building", "label": "First extension", "value": "$150,000"}, {"icon": "building", "label": "Second extension", "value": "$350,000 more"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.43, 0.92, 1.35, 1.55, 1.84, 2.17, 2.56, 2.91, 3.03, 3.59]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "A second extension required another $350,000.", "t0": 20.97, "t1": 24.22, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Second extension"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.87, 1.32, 1.64, 1.9, 2.19, 2.49, 2.84]}, {"scene": "earlier", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "An earlier audit found the café omitted a surcharge from gross revenue.", "t0": 24.44, "t1": 27.81, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "historical", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "2011 through 2013 revenue audit", "mark": "2011 through 2013 revenue audit"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.52, 0.81, 1.01, 1.11, 1.56, 1.92, 2.01, 2.53, 2.69, 2.99]}, {"scene": "earlier", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The audit counted $248,029 in omitted revenue across those earlier years.", "t0": 27.93, "t1": 33.02, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$248,029", "label": "Gross revenue omitted from 2011 through 2013"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.43, 0.76, 1.0, 1.28, 1.74, 2.11, 2.63, 2.98, 3.1, 3.45, 3.84, 4.15, 4.37, 4.73]}, {"scene": "earlier", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "Auditors calculated $16,987 in unpaid rent, plus interest.", "t0": 33.14, "t1": 38.21, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Earlier audit, separate from 2026 arrears", "heading": "Percentage rent and interest", "source": "historical", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Unpaid rent", "value": "$16,987"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "Interest", "value": "$8,154"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 1.04, 1.48, 1.89, 2.09, 2.34, 2.89, 3.25, 3.36, 3.74, 4.35, 4.67]}, {"scene": "earlier", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The café said it corrected the surcharge calculation.", "t0": 38.33, "t1": 40.89, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Café response"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.55, 0.74, 0.84, 1.27, 1.38, 1.87]}, {"scene": "earlier", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The Controller later marked those earlier recommendations closed.", "t0": 41.01, "t1": 43.87, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "historicClosure", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "2019 closure report", "mark": "2019 closure report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.6, 0.89, 1.13, 1.34, 1.67, 2.41]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The draft gives the first extension 120 months and the second 60 months.", "t0": 44.09, "t1": 47.92, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "lease", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors, file 260948", "text": "Draft lease", "mark": "Draft lease"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.61, 0.71, 0.97, 1.47, 1.66, 1.92, 2.2, 2.54, 2.74, 2.86, 3.2, 3.52]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The adopted resolution reverses that order, giving five years first, then ten.", "t0": 48.04, "t1": 51.99, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "final", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors, file 260948", "text": "Resolution 543-26", "mark": "Resolution 543-26"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.57, 1.17, 1.63, 1.82, 2.23, 2.54, 2.81, 3.06, 3.35, 3.56]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Both reach 2045. The order affects when a market rent reset would occur.", "t0": 52.11, "t1": 56.27, "shot": "r13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Market rent reset"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.48, 0.77, 1.71, 1.89, 2.16, 2.49, 2.64, 2.74, 3.09, 3.32, 3.65, 3.82]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "The analyst said the projected base revenue figure needed to come down.", "t0": 56.39, "t1": 59.55, "shot": "r14", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "budget", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors, file 260948", "text": "Legislative analyst recommendation", "mark": "Legislative analyst recommendation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.54, 0.77, 0.88, 1.34, 1.61, 1.96, 2.26, 2.51, 2.61, 2.82]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "The amended authorization reduced the figure to 3,236,685 dollars and waived competitive bidding.", "t0": 59.67, "t1": 65.19, "shot": "r15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "final", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors, file 260948", "text": "Resolution 543-26", "mark": "Resolution 543-26"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.5, 1.24, 1.58, 1.69, 1.98, 2.15, 2.44, 2.71, 2.99, 3.25, 3.59, 4.02, 4.33, 4.67, 5.18]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["defense[0]"], "text": "Port staff cited weak sales and the risks of litigation and an empty property.", "t0": 65.31, "t1": 69.09, "shot": "r16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The Port’s position"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.54, 0.86, 1.09, 1.4, 1.5, 1.63, 1.88, 1.97, 2.66, 2.92, 3.02, 3.28]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "What would an open bid have produced? One way to test that is to compare actual offers.", "t0": 69.21, "t1": 73.59, "shot": "r17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Market rent", "Final recovery"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.34, 0.44, 0.72, 0.93, 1.04, 1.98, 2.22, 2.39, 2.5, 2.75, 2.93, 3.04, 3.14, 3.55, 3.99]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 73.71, "t1": 75.91, "shot": "r18", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.36, 0.47, 0.54, 1.22, 1.44, 1.53]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"lease": "Rent and an extension", "earlier": "What the earlier audit measured", "review": "The revenue estimate"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "question"}